# Hook is in the hands of code that nobody has seen and has no class, so the read of `touch` off it is closed. It stands in one turn of four, in the copy of Below, and that turn comes round in the typed copy of the loop; the other turns are quiet.
# Code that nobody has seen calls run, so its own body runs. At its second read the getter behind `touch` takes away what one guard of the loop stands for. The turns behind it go by what is there now.
# RUN: walk f4 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: PropGet {{*}} key="touch"
# CHECK: = AreMembersUnchanged conditions=[{layout=L1 key="second"}]
